Leader is `Space`. Escape in insert/cmdline: `jj`

Files and search (fzf.vim)
--------------------------
- `<leader>o`    : Files (`<leader>O` fullscreen)
- `<leader>b`    : Buffers (jumps to an open window)
- `<leader>rg`   : Rg (ripgrep)
- `<leader>gls`  : GFiles (git ls-files)
- `<leader>gs`   : GFiles? (git status)
- `<leader>;`    : Commands     `<leader>``  : Marks
- `<leader>t`    : Tags         `<leader>T`  : BTags (visual: selected text)
- `<leader>l`    : BLines (lines in this buffer)
- `<leader><tab>`: Search mappings
- `ctrl-p`       : In `:` cmdline, command History
- `F1`           : Helptags
- `ctrl-x ctrl-f`: Insert mode, complete path (`ctrl-x ctrl-l` line, `ctrl-x ctrl-k` word if /usr/share/dict/words exists)

Buffers, windows, files
-----------------------
- `<leader>j` / `<leader>k` : Previous / next buffer
- `<leader>x`  : Close buffer, keep window
- `ctrl-h/j/k/l` : Move to left/down/up/right window
- `<leader>nt` : Toggle NERDTree (`I` toggles hidden files)
- `<leader>w` `:w`, `<leader>wa` `:wa`, `<leader>W` sudo save
- `<leader>q` `:q`, `<leader>Q` `:q!`, `<leader>qa` `:qa`

Editing
-------
- `H` / `L`    : Start / end of line      `Y` : Yank to end of line
- `Enter`      : Break line (normal mode) `ctrl-e` : End of line (insert mode)
- `=`          : Toggle comment (nerdcommenter)
- `<leader>rw` : Replace word under cursor everywhere (visual: selection)
- `<leader>/`  : Search for the visual selection
- `<leader>hw` / `<leader>hW` : Highlight word under cursor on / off
- `<leader>noh`: Clear search highlight
- `<leader>.`  : Play macro `q` (record with `qq`)

Git and toggles
---------------
- `]c` / `[c`  : Next / previous hunk (gitgutter default)
- `<leader>hp` / `<leader>hs` / `<leader>hu` : Preview / stage / undo hunk (gitgutter default)
- `:Git` / `:G`: fugitive (no custom maps)
- `<leader>d`  : Toggle diff for this window
- `F4` numbers, `F5` gitgutter, `F6` strip whitespace on save, `F7` paste
- `<leader>cd` : lcd to file dir   `<leader>ev` : Edit vimrc
- `<leader>md` : Toggle Markdown preview (Markdown files)
